### 4.3 What the city template gives

From the XML records (appendix):
- **Town Essentials**, the human's first building in a city in both games (the AIs build
  Walls or the Obelisk first):
  - land-unit production `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:TOWN_ESSENTIALS:DomainProductionModifiers}}`;
  - gold `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:TOWN_ESSENTIALS:CommerceModifiers}}` per cent;
  - a merchant slot.
- **City Essentials**, built in nearly every city within a few turns of City Planning; the AIs
  build it in a minority of their cities:
  - the same land-unit production `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:CITY_ESSENTIALS:DomainProductionModifiers}}`;
  - gold `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:CITY_ESSENTIALS:CommerceModifiers}}` per cent;
  - merchant slots `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:CITY_ESSENTIALS:SpecialistCounts}}`.
- **The Forge**, early in the order in nearly every city the human founded:
  - production bonuses from metal resources, `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:FORGE:BonusYieldModifiers}}`;
  - an engineer slot.
- **The trade buildings:**
  - River Port: trade routes `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:RIVER_PORT:iTradeRoutes}}`, route yield
    `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:RIVER_PORT:iTradeRouteModifier}}` per cent;
  - Roman Forum: route yield `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:ROMAN_FORUM:iTradeRouteModifier}}` per cent,
    gold `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:ROMAN_FORUM:CommerceModifiers}}` per cent;
  - Jewellery: route yield `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:JEWELLERY:iTradeRouteModifier}}` per cent;
  - Port: trade routes `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:PORT:iTradeRoutes}}`, route yield
    `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:PORT:iTradeRouteModifier}}` per cent.
- **The Courthouse**, in most cities soon after Code of Laws (the AIs build almost none):
  maintenance `{{eff:st.game4_building_template:COURTHOUSE:iMaintenanceModifier}}` per cent.
- **The military buildings come last:** Barracks, Early Barracks, Legion Barracks, Stable, Siege
  Workshop. They are built in most cities only in the war phases, one or two turns after their
  tech.
- **Wonders.** The human builds world wonders only late, after the city template is in place: a
  religious shrine in game 3, and in game 4 the Roman wonders of the last phases, which then
  outnumber any single AI's (section 4.2). It does not race for early wonders; its production
  goes first into the city template and units.

### 4.4 The result, at the save

{{table:st.game3_city_profile}}

{{table:st.game4_city_profile}}

The human's ordinary founded cities make more hammers and commerce than the AIs' capitals, and
have more trade routes and many more buildings than the AIs' other cities. Captured cities are
behind: in game 4 most were taken in the last turns.

